            "review_title": "Review at Banh Mi 362",
            "review_text": "Tee\nSydney, Australia192 contributions\n0\n#1 Banh Mi in Vietnam\nFeb 2018 • Couples\nThis was the first Banh Mi we tried when arriving to HCMC. Bread was perfect - crunchy exterior with pillow-like dough inside. The meat, pate, vegetables and chilli were fresh and filling with just right right amount of heat. For 30,000d ($1.70 AUD) this was the perfect way to begin our Vietnam adventure. \n\nTrekking up the coast to Hanoi, we sampled each city’s take on the famous baguette almost every day over a month, and I’m surprised to say that Banh Mi 362 was equally my favourite - in tie with Hoi An’s Madam Khanh! A highlight to our stay in HCMC.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 23, 2018",
